---
// The benchmark whitepaper. Every figure here is from the paper in assets/whitepaper/, which is served as written.
import fs from 'node:fs'
import path from 'node:path'
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro'
import { Icon } from '@astrojs/starlight/components'
import { WHITEPAPER_HTML, WHITEPAPER_PDF, WHITEPAPER_ROUTE } from '../../../scripts/whitepaper.mjs'

// Resolved when the page renders. import.meta.url is the bundled chunk by then, so the site root is the build's cwd.
const pdfBytes = fs.statSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), '..', 'assets', 'whitepaper', WHITEPAPER_PDF)).size
const pdfSize = `${(pdfBytes / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1)} MB`

const readUrl = WHITEPAPER_ROUTE + WHITEPAPER_HTML
const pdfUrl = WHITEPAPER_ROUTE + WHITEPAPER_PDF

const figures = [
    { value: '30.4%', text: 'of the tokens used by the next most efficient platform: 1.92M against 6.32M across 36 runs.' },
    { value: '36 / 36', text: 'runs passed on Cuttlely. A pass is a completion check, not a correctness grade.' },
    { value: '$0.34', text: 'for all 36 runs at list prices, about half the cost of the next two platforms.' }
]
---

<StarlightPage
    frontmatter={{
        title: 'Lean context, reliable agents',
        description:
            'The Cuttlely benchmark whitepaper: same agent, a third of the tokens, zero failed runs. One production agent workload rebuilt in four platforms, with the method and its limits.',
        template: 'splash',
        pagefind: true,
        tableOfContents: false,
        prev: false,
        next: false
    }}
    hasSidebar={false}
>
    <div class="cl-home not-content">
        <section class="cl-section cl-center" aria-labelledby="whitepaper-title">
            <p class="cl-kicker">Benchmark whitepaper · October 2026</p>
            <h2 id="whitepaper-title" class="cl-display">Same agent, a third of the tokens, zero failed runs.</h2>
            <p class="cl-lead">
                An AI assistant workload from a real production deployment, rebuilt natively in four platforms and run on the same model, tools and
                questions: 36 runs per platform. The paper compares token use and run reliability, and explains its method and caveats.
            </p>
            <div class="cl-actions cl-actions-center">
                <a class="cl-button cl-button-primary" href={readUrl}>Read the whitepaper <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a>
                <a class="cl-button cl-button-ghost" href={pdfUrl} download>
                    <Icon name="download" /> Download the PDF ({pdfSize})
                </a>
            </div>
            <ul class="cl-installs cl-whitepaper-figures">
                {
                    figures.map((item) => (
                        <li>
                            <a href={readUrl + '#results'}>
                                <span class="cl-display">{item.value}</span>
                                <span>{item.text}</span>
                            </a>
                        </li>
                    ))
                }
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="cl-section cl-center" aria-labelledby="whitepaper-inside-title">
            <h2 id="whitepaper-inside-title" class="cl-display">Inside</h2>
            <p>
                The executive summary and thesis, the problem of context cost, the method, the results, why fewer tokens means more reliable answers, the
                architecture, the limitations, and how to reproduce the runs.
            </p>
            <p class="cl-center">
                <a class="cl-link-arrow" href="/docs/how-to/context-and-tokens/">How Cuttlely keeps context small <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a>
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
    .cl-whitepaper-figures {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 12rem), 1fr));
    }
</style>
